---
// NOT a violation, and the only file in this fixture whose job is to be allowed. It
// imports the choke point exactly as src/pages/direct.astro next to it does — same one-hop
// edge, same target — and differs in one respect: it is named in FIXTURE_AUTH_CONSUMERS in
// tests/anonymous-read-path.test.ts. The pair is what proves the allowlist is doing the
// work. If the exemption stopped being consulted, this page would be reported and the
// "reports exactly those eight importers" assertion would find nine; if the exemption
// leaked to everything, direct.astro would stop being reported and it would find seven.
//
// It also stands in for what a real entry will look like: a page that renders something
// for a signed-in person, rendered on the server, never hydrated. That last part is not
// decoration — it is the condition Invariant D checks, and this file passing it is what
// case (c) means. Its sibling src/components/AllowlistedIsland.vue is the same exemption
// granted to a module that does NOT satisfy it.
import '../lib/auth/index';
---

